 "result_text": "I fixed the duplicate `[None]` sections, but I haven't run the tests or tried it against a real login.\n\nWhen no profile was set, the code still wrote the credentials to disk under the profile name `None`. Each run added another `[None]` section, which is what made aws-cli throw `DuplicateSectionError`.\n\nIn `aws_google_auth/__init__.py`, `_store` is now only called when a profile is set. With no profile, the tool just prints the `export ...` line and writes nothing to `~/.aws`.\n\nAny `[None]` sections already in your credentials file will still be there. You'll need to delete those by hand.\n\nThe file changed on disk after my edit. I didn't read the new contents, so I haven't checked that my change is still intact.",
